<<declare $gh_met_harbourmaster = false>>
<<declare $gh_heard_missing_boat_warning = false>>
<<declare $gh_accepted_sounding_job = false>>
<<declare $gh_asked_about_bell = false>>
<<declare $gh_harbourmaster_trust = 0>>
<<declare $gh_met_mara = false>>
<<declare $gh_mara_trust = 0>>
<<declare $gh_met_tomas = false>>
<<declare $gh_tomas_trust = 0>>
<<declare $gh_met_inez = false>>
<<declare $gh_inez_trust = 0>>


title: Greyhaven_Harbourmaster
---
<<if not $gh_met_harbourmaster>>
Harbourmaster: You're the new hand on the old boat, then.
Harbourmaster: Keep her inside the buoys until you know how the channel behaves.
<<else>>
Harbourmaster: Back already? The channel has not become any kinder.
<<endif>>

-> Ask about the missing boats.
    <<if not $gh_heard_missing_boat_warning>>
        <<set $gh_heard_missing_boat_warning = true>>
        Harbourmaster: Three boats went out past the outer marker. Only one came back.
        Harbourmaster: Its skipper would not speak about what followed him.
        Harbourmaster: He kept asking whether the bell was still ringing.
    <<else>>
        Harbourmaster: The same three boats. The same one that returned. Nobody has found the other two.
    <<endif>>
    -> Ask about the bell.
        <<set $gh_asked_about_bell = true>>
        Harbourmaster: The lighthouse bell? It has been silent for eleven years.
        Harbourmaster: Do not answer a bell you cannot place.
        <<set $gh_harbourmaster_trust = $gh_harbourmaster_trust + 1>>
    -> Leave the subject alone.
        Harbourmaster: Sensible. The sea has enough listeners.

-> Ask for work.
    <<if not $gh_accepted_sounding_job>>
        Harbourmaster: A sounding buoy washed in near the western mudflat.
        Harbourmaster: Bring it back intact. Do not switch it on.
        Harbourmaster: If it starts answering, drop the line.
        <<set $gh_accepted_sounding_job = true>>
        <<checkpoint "greyhaven.sounding_buoy_accepted">>
    <<else>>
        Harbourmaster: The western mudflat. Bring the buoy back intact. And keep it switched off.
    <<endif>>

-> Ask about the channel.
    Harbourmaster: The western channel is shallow at ebb. The eastern marker lies over broken stone.
    Harbourmaster: Keep your engine low near the mangroves. The water carries sound there.

-> Say nothing.
    Harbourmaster: Then listen before you leave.

<<set $gh_met_harbourmaster = true>>
===

title: Greyhaven_Fishmonger
---
<<if not $gh_met_mara>>
Mara Venn: If you're here to sell, put the catch down gently. I can tell a rough landing by the bruises.
Mara Venn: First time at my stall? Mara. I keep the market open while there's something worth weighing.
<<else>>
Mara Venn: Back with another hold of surprises? Let me see what the water gave you.
<<endif>>
-> Ask about the fish.
    Mara Venn: Most of what comes through here is ordinary. Mullet, milkfish, sillago. They smell like the sea should.
    Mara Venn: Lately, a few catches arrive cold in the middle. Not spoiled. Just cold, as if they were lifted from deeper water.
    <<set $gh_mara_trust = $gh_mara_trust + 1>>
-> Ask about the missing boats.
    Mara Venn: One of the missing crews owed me for ice. I still set aside their crate every morning.
    Mara Venn: Habit is a stubborn thing. Hope is worse.
-> Ask about selling unusual catches.
    Mara Venn: Don't hide a strange catch from the person weighing it. I won't promise a good price, but I won't pretend I didn't see it.
-> Leave.
    Mara Venn: Keep the catch shaded. Sun ruins good work faster than a bad buyer.
<<set $gh_met_mara = true>>
===

title: Greyhaven_Mechanic
---
<<if not $gh_met_tomas>>
Tomas Vale: Stop there. I want to hear that engine idle before you tell me what's wrong with it.
Tomas Vale: Tomas. I keep the repair shed running. Mostly engines, sometimes boats, occasionally bad decisions.
<<else>>
Tomas Vale: That engine still sounds like it has something to confess.
<<endif>>
-> Ask about repairs.
    Tomas Vale: Bring her in before the hull starts taking water. A small repair is cheap. A tow from the outer marker isn't.
    <<set $gh_tomas_trust = $gh_tomas_trust + 1>>
-> Ask about strange noises beneath boats.
    Tomas Vale: I've heard knocks travel through a hull. Loose fittings, trapped timber, a line caught under the keel. There are explanations.
    Tomas Vale: The trouble starts when the knocking keeps pace with the engine.
-> Ask about the missing boats.
    Tomas Vale: The boat that came back had fresh scoring under the waterline. No matching scrape on the rocks. I logged it as unknown damage.
-> Leave.
    Tomas Vale: Don't ignore a change in engine pitch. The boat usually tells you before it quits.
<<set $gh_met_tomas = true>>
===

title: Greyhaven_NetMender
---
<<if not $gh_met_inez>>
Inez Sarmiento: Mind the mesh. A torn net can be mended. A careless knot can lose the whole catch.
Inez Sarmiento: Inez. If your lines come back cut clean, bring them to me. Don't decide what did it before you look.
<<else>>
Inez Sarmiento: Show me the line. I can tell a snag from a cut if there's enough left to examine.
<<endif>>
-> Ask about the nets.
    Inez Sarmiento: Reef stone frays a line. Propellers shred it. But some of the recovered nets have cuts that begin on the inside.
    <<set $gh_inez_trust = $gh_inez_trust + 1>>
-> Ask about the missing crews.
    Inez Sarmiento: One crew used to tie three turns around the float line before leaving harbour. Their gear came back with every knot still fastened.
    Inez Sarmiento: The net was empty. Not torn. Empty.
-> Ask about local rules.
    Inez Sarmiento: If the birds leave the water all at once, don't follow the fish. Check the wind. Check the current. Then decide whether you still want to be out there.
-> Leave.
    Inez Sarmiento: Bring the damaged line back. Don't throw away evidence just because it frightens you.
<<set $gh_met_inez = true>>
===
